# The demo build (demo/Dockerfile, context: repo root) does `COPY . .`,
# which is not governed by .gitignore — Docker copies whatever is on disk
# regardless of what git tracks. Found the expensive way: a local go.work
# (untracked, per .gitignore, and recommended by RELEASING.md for normal
# development) leaked into the build image and set a Go version floor the
# pinned build image did not satisfy, failing a build that has nothing to
# do with go.work at all — cmd/crierd's own go.mod is what actually governs
# it. Anything here is a real go.work someone made pinned to whatever they
# were working on when they built the demo.
go.work
go.work.sum

# Never useful inside a build, and a full repo clone's worth of git history
# is a poor trade for however many megabytes it happens to be.
.git/

# Same reasoning as .gitignore: never build inputs.
.DS_Store
.env
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov
